# Day 25

## Experiment Title

Using Environment Variables in Docker Compose


## Objective

To understand how environment variables are configured and used in Docker Compose applications.


## Theory

Environment variables are used to configure application settings dynamically without modifying the application source code. Docker Compose allows environment variables to be defined directly inside the docker-compose.yml file.

These variables are commonly used for database credentials, application ports, usernames, passwords, and other configuration settings. Environment variables make containerized applications more flexible and easier to manage.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and verify that Docker services are running properly.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file with environment variable settings.

Configure the required variables for the application service.

Start the Docker Compose application.

Verify that the container initializes successfully using the configured variables.

Check the running container configuration and logs.


## Output

Environment variables were successfully configured in the Docker Compose application.

The application container initialized correctly using the provided configuration values.

Docker Compose managed the environment settings successfully.


## Result

Successfully learned how to configure and use environment variables in Docker Compose applications.
